    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-l/q9",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q9-question-1.svg\" alt=\"B 5 m ϕ A The figure above shows a ladder AB resting in equilibrium with one end A on rough horizontal ground and the other end B against a smooth vertical wall. The ladder is modelled as a uniform rod of length 5 metres and mass 20 kg, and lies in a vertical plane perpendicular to the wall and the ground, inclined at an angle ϕ to the\" style=\"--madas-width:560.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q9-question-2.svg\" alt=\"horizontal. When a person, which is modelled as a particle, of mass 60 kg stands at a point C on the ladder, where AC = 4 metres the ladder is at the point of slipping. Given that the coefficient of friction between the ladder and the ground is 1 4 , find … a) … the magnitude of the frictional force of the ground on the ladder. ( ) 1 b) … the value of ϕ , to the nearest degree. ( ) 5\" style=\"--madas-width:586.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q9-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Starting with a diagram: (a) Vertical equilibrium gives the ground’s normal reaction R = 80g.\" style=\"--madas-width:448.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"At limiting equilibrium, F = R/4 = 20g = 196 N . [A1] (b) Horizontally the wall reaction equals F. [B1] Taking moments about A, the clockwise and anticlockwise moments balance: (20g · 2.5 + 60g · 4) cos φ = 20g · 5 sin φ. [M1] [A1] Cancel g, collect 50 + 240 = 290 on the left and 20(5) = 100 on the right, and divide 290 cos φ = 100 sin φ by 100 cos φ. Hence tan φ = 2.9, [A1] giving φ = 71◦to the nearest degree: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 9 is 6 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "B 5 m ϕ A The figure above shows a ladder AB resting in equilibrium with one end A on rough horizontal ground and the other end B against a smooth vertical wall. The ladder is modelled as a uniform rod of length 5 metres and mass 20 kg, and lies in a vertical plane perpendicular to the wall and the ground, inclined at an angle ϕ to the horizontal. When a person, which is modelled as a particle, of mass 60 kg stands at a point C on the ladder, where AC = 4 metres the ladder is at the point of slipping. Given that the coefficient of friction between the ladder and the ground is 1 4 , find … a) … the magnitude of the frictional force of the ground on the ladder. ( ) 1 b) … the value of ϕ , to the nearest degree. ( ) 5"
