    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-l/q10",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q10-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A particle is projected from a point O on level horizontal ground with speed of ms− at an angle β to the horizontal, where 1 12 45.5 tan β = . 5 The particle is moving freely under gravity, reaching a greatest height of H m above the ground before it lands on the ground at a point P . a) Find the flight time of the particle. ( ) 4 b) Hence determine the distance OP and the value of H . ( ) 4 c) Determine the speed of the particle 4 seconds after leaving O . ( ) 4\" style=\"--madas-width:570.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q10-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:588.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q10-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Looking at the vertical motion from O to P The 5-12-13 triangle gives the initial horizontal and vertical components 17.5 and 42 m s−1. (a) The vertical launch velocity is 45.5(12/13) = 42 m s−1. [B1] At landing the vertical displacement is zero, so 42t −4.9t2 = 0. [A1] Factorising gives t(42 −4.9t) = 0. [M1] The positive root is\" style=\"--madas-width:666.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q10-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"60/7 s ≈8.57 s . [A1] (b) Looking at the horizontal motion The horizontal acceleration is zero, so the speed stays at 45.5(5/13) = 17.5 m s−1 throughout the flight: The range is 17.5(60/7) = 150 m . [M1] [A1] At the highest point the vertical velocity is zero, so 0 = 422 −19.6H, [A1] giving H = 90 m . [A1] Alternative for the height. By symmetry the highest point is reached at half the flight time, 30/7 seconds: Then H = 42(30/7) −4.9(30/7)2 = 90 m. (c)\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q10-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"At t = 4 the vertical velocity is 42 −9.8(4) = 2.8 m s−1. [B1] [A1] The speed is 17.52 + 2.82 ≈17.72 m s−1 . p [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 10 is 12 marks.</p>"
    ],
