  {
    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-l/q11",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q11-question-1.svg\" alt=\"P A B Two particles A and B of respective masses 2 kg and 5 kg are attached to the ends of a light inextensible string which passes over a smooth pulley P . The two particles are held at rest, at the same level above a horizontal floor with the portions of the strings not in contact with the pulley vertical. The system is then released from rest.\" style=\"--madas-width:558.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q11-question-2.svg\" alt=\"a) For the period before B reaches the floor, calculate in any order … i. … the acceleration of the system. ii. … the tension in the string. ( ) 5 Eventually B reaches the floor 0.5 s after release and does not rebound. In the ensuing motion A does not reach P . b) Determine the greatest height of A above the floor. ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:589.5px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q11-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) With A rising and B descending at acceleration magnitude a, Newton’s second law gives T −2g = 2a [M1] and 5g −T = 5a. [A1] Adding both particle equations eliminates T, leaving 5g −2g = (2 + 5)a. Substitute a = 4.2 in T = 2g + 2a to get 19.6 + 8.4 = 28. Adding gives a = 3g/7 = 4.2 m s−2 , [M1] [A1] followed by\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
