      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q15-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The first segment covers 6.25(120) = 750 m. [M1] The rest segment adds zero distance. [A1] The final segment covers 750 m between t = 150 [A1] and t = 240, [A1] and since its velocity is constant it covers 750(60/90) = 500 m [A1] in the final 60 seconds: [A1] For the final straight section the magnitude of the gradient is 750/90 = 25/3 m s−1; reversing direction contributes positive distance 60(25/3) = 500. The average speed is 750 + 750 + 500 = 20 3 m s−1 ≈6.67 m s−1 . [M1] [A1] 300\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
