    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-l/q16-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) The displacement in four hours is 20i + 44j in kilometres: [B1] The velocity is (5i + 11j) km h−1 . [M1] [A1] (b) At time t the positions in kilometres are rP = (5t −11)i + (11t −24)j, rQ = 5i + (8t −10)j. [B1] Initial position of the first particle [B1] add its velocity times elapsed time [B1] initial position of the second particle [B1] add its velocity times elapsed time Therefore d2 = (5t −16)2 + (3t −14)2 = 34t2 −244t + 452 . [M1] [M1] [A1] (c) The visibility boundary d = 10 [B1] gives 17t2 −122t + 176 = 0, or (t −2)(17t −88) = 0. [A1] Expansion gives 25t2 −160t + 256 + 9t2 −84t + 196 = 100.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
